#~ shadowed_header
# fixedbugs, defect d-lane-blocking-small-2 (2026-11-24): `stdint.h` beside
# the program is a link to a device, `/dev/null` (made in the case's copy,
# `links`), in the folder the build searches before the system's, and the
# program binds no header: the runtime's own opening reads `<stdint.h>`. A
# FIFO there hung `heroes build` in clang's first listing until it was
# killed. Every file the opening reaches is now walked before any clang
# starts, and the build is refused at the program's first byte, as a file
# standing in for the library's header is, with what stands there.

function main()
    print(1)
